# Kimi-K3 Workflow

Apply this rule whenever a task concerns Kimi-K3, SGLang K3, AITER K3,
MXFP4, MLA/KDA, or the associated benchmark artifacts.

1. Read `/workspace/claude-skills/kimi-k3/HANDOFF_2026-08-21.md` first,
   especially `CONTINUE HERE`.
2. Treat that handoff, `/workspace/claude-skills/kimi-k3/SUMMARY.md`, and
   linked tracker reports as the source of truth. Do not reconstruct old chats.
3. Check both worktrees before editing:
   - `/sgl-workspace/sglang-k3-triton37`
   - `/sgl-workspace/aiter-k3-triton37`
4. Preserve all pre-existing uncommitted changes. Never reset, discard,
   overwrite, commit, or push unless the user explicitly requests it.
5. Distinguish prior MXFP4 work from the manually ported PR #35770 attention
   changes. Do not remove one while intending to remove the other.
6. Production currently remains on AITER prefill with Triton decode.
   `SGLANG_K3_TRITON_PREFILL_PROFILE` defaults to `off`; do not change the
   default without new endpoint and correctness evidence.
7. Record durable decisions, metrics, exact revisions, commands, and next
   steps under `/workspace/claude-skills/kimi-k3/`.
8. Keep a concise `CONTINUE HERE` section and update the handoff before ending
   a long optimization session.
